              "ref": "D3",
              "type": "str",
              "value": "A letter-position algorithm is inherently witness-sensitive. But 4Q11, our closest biblical witness for Exod 14:19–21, reflects the short MT/LXX literary form and its extant consonants in these verses are close to MT; lacunae prevent a full independent 216-letter recount.",
              "raw_value": "A letter-position algorithm is inherently witness-sensitive. But 4Q11, our closest biblical witness for Exod 14:19–21, reflects the short MT/LXX literary form and its extant consonants in these verses are close to MT; lacunae prevent a full independent 216-letter recount.",
